    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Llama's gated MLP previously left down-projection output at the linear backends' FP16 default. Widening that result only after projection cannot recover a value already overflowed during FP16 output storage.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_0940ed7aa3f94007a0cb63fcf32185de",
          "call_d029f6676b294405ad07b4f50d918020",
          "call_b7016771323a488d9cb2ce48d157966e",
          "call_4e10dc2e257044d79a0509724b42e2e2"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The one-line change requests torch.float at GatedMLP construction. Existing plumbing carries this choice into every down projection before its output is allocated, rather than merely casting the completed MLP result.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_af5f80db7c6142d992160849f685e6f2",
          "call_d029f6676b294405ad07b4f50d918020",
          "call_2639054d91a648ab9ce16e66054e3bc7"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "This is a targeted numerical behavior change: down outputs and sliced-down accumulation become FP32, while gate/up computation, attention output precision and the already-FP32 residual stream are unchanged.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_af5f80db7c6142d992160849f685e6f2",
          "call_d029f6676b294405ad07b4f50d918020",
          "call_63874a9c58c9434d876cb16be08380f6",
          "call_adc86504442b4808b03f2bd3c200eebe",
          "call_ca2ecd4e0b8743eca69aab2abee4ae85"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "Read the initial commit's models and modules chapters and the cache-construction entry 4fa0e686. They establish the shared constructor, module sequence, FP32 embedding default and residual-storage design. The initial models chapter also records a Mistral sliding-window mapping gap; inspection of the current Mistral/Llama constructors and this diff shows that omission is carried over, not corrected by this precision change.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_9b21fe72a58140e793b0857c5911a1db",
          "call_b5d23e517ef043359c228540d9e732b5",
          "call_3e01ae6a180747fbaa70503a228fba84"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The task changes only the GatedMLP constructor argument. Mistral still supplies no sliding-window adaptation, and Llama's Attention construction still omits sliding_window, whose default is -1.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_bf4ab54222034bd39cfedeb313ba3802",
          "call_0940ed7aa3f94007a0cb63fcf32185de",
          "call_ca2ecd4e0b8743eca69aab2abee4ae85",
          "call_af5f80db7c6142d992160849f685e6f2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Other inspected discussions have different framing: \u201ctorch._C._LinAlgError on last layer of quant\u201d concerns Command-A and suspected activation overflow; \u201cconverting to 3.0 bpw causes error; block state has 0 inf values and 34 NaN values\u201d includes Midnight-Miqu and Command-R+ reports. Their relationship to this task is inference from shared conversion errors and linear.py references, not evidence of an identical cause. \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate\u201d reports an extension-import/toolchain problem; \u201c`RuntimeError` when requesting logprobs with Gemma 3 models\u201d reports a tensor-size mismatch. Neither establishes a down-output overflow.",
        "basis": "inference",
